// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6647 new: Potential Cloud Access Token Or Secret Retrieval Via Cloud CLI
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6647
// Pull request author: elhoim
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Cloud Access Token Or Secret Retrieval Via Cloud CLI
// Sigma ID: b98a5770-14ad-484b-8575-ba00fdd37d91
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2026-11-18 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1528, T1552, T1552.001
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects command lines of cloud and Kubernetes CLIs (gcloud, az, azd, aws, gh, kubectl), or of a
//   shell or interpreter wrapping them, that print a usable access token, export the configured
//   credentials or dump stored secrets in clear text. Attackers who land on a developer workstation
//   or a CI runner run these commands to harvest the tokens cached by the logged-in CLI sessions
//   instead of stealing credential files from disk, as the compromised Nx npm package did with "gh
//   auth token". These commands are common on developer machines and in automation. Use the rule for
//   hunting and baseline the known identities, parent processes and runner images.
// False positives:
//   - Developers, administrators and platform engineers retrieve tokens and secrets with these commands as part of their daily work
//   - CI/CD runners, infrastructure-as-code tools, credential helpers and IDE extensions that obtain tokens from the local CLI session
//   - Google credential helpers (docker-credential-gcloud, gke-gcloud-auth-plugin) running "gcloud config config-helper", and Terraform providers running "az account get-access-token"
// References:
//   - https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/f4ef34b1c996da53880053dd497ca546c1b0bbfa/rules/cross-platform/credential_access_multi_cloud_cli_token_harvesting.toml
//   - https://www.stepsecurity.io/blog/supply-chain-security-alert-popular-nx-build-system-package-compromised-with-data-stealing-malware
//   - https://cloud.google.com/sdk/gcloud/reference/auth/print-access-token
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/account?view=azure-cli-latest#az-account-get-access-token
//   - https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_auth_token
//   - https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/configure/export-credentials.html
//   - https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubectl/generated/kubectl_config/kubectl_config_view/
//   - https://socket.dev/blog/nx-packages-compromised
//   - https://www.trendmicro.com/en/research/25/k/shai-hulud-2-0-targets-cloud-and-developer-systems.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/bae73446f52232e4882fa82ac0cd72aa4bab315c/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cloud_cli_token_and_secret_retrieval.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "auth print-access-token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "auth print-identity-token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "application-default print-access-token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "config config-helper" or ProcessCommandLine contains "secrets versions access" or ProcessCommandLine contains "account get-access-token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Get-AzAccessToken" or ProcessCommandLine contains "keyvault secret show" or ProcessCommandLine contains " auth token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "auth status --show-token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "sts get-session-token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "sts assume-role" or ProcessCommandLine contains "sts get-federation-token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "configure export-credentials" or ProcessCommandLine contains "configure get aws_secret_access_key" or ProcessCommandLine contains "configure get aws_session_token" or ProcessCommandLine contains "secretsmanager get-secret-value") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "config view" and ProcessCommandLine contains "--raw") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "get secret" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-o json" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-o yaml" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-o=json" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-o=yaml" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-ojson" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-oyaml" or ProcessCommandLine contains "go-template" or ProcessCommandLine contains "jsonpath" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--output"))
